-- title:
--   Lemma 4.3 — positive perturbation and transfer
-- statement:
--   Let $n\ge2$ and $p_1\ge\cdots\ge p_n\ge0$ sum to one. Define $q_i=(p_i+e^{-n})/(1+ne^{-n})$. Then $q$ is a strictly positive probability vector with the same weak ordering as $p$. From every common initial list and for every integer $t\ge0$,
--   $$\mathbb E_pF_p(X_t)\le\mathbb E_qF_q(Y_t)+(t+1)n^2e^{-n}.$$
--   For the stationary probability constructed from $q$,
--   $$H_q=\log(1/\min_\sigma\mu_q(\sigma))\le n^3/2.$$
--   Each marginal is generated by its own request distribution. This transfers the finite-time estimate to vectors with zeros.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: labels and charged positions 1 through n → labels and positions Fin n with charged position val + 1; reason: the order-preserving shift gives a bijection of all labels and list states
--   - encoding: decreasing relabeling with OPT equal to the sorted positional cost → OPT is the attained minimum over all permutations; reason: sorting shows these are identical, including ties and zeros; no label order is required by the goal
--   - encoding: IID requests and the state after t steps → the explicit request kernel raised to the natural power t; reason: finite matrix products give exactly the IID marginal law; nonnegative integer times are Nat
-- source:
--   Clayton Mizgerd, Transposition achieves OPT+O(1) in polynomial time for IID list update, STOC 2027 submission #668 (October 2026), supplied canonical submission artifact; citation basis published (not acceptance). Lemma 4.3, printed p.10 = PDF p.10; source.pdf SHA256 07dbf227a79b9907070bc1c27f25a0848cee3135ec65bcf105159f991b3b4545.

import Definitions.Def_TranspositionIID_Main_Perturbation

namespace TranspositionIID.Main

/-- Lemma 4.3, printed/PDF p.10, including every conclusion of (4.5) and (4.6). -/
theorem lemma_4_3 {n : ℕ} (hn : 2 ≤ n) (p : Fin n → ℝ)
    (hp : ActuarialValuation.isFiniteStateDistribution p) (hsort : Decreasing p) :
    ActuarialValuation.isFiniteStateDistribution (perturb p) ∧
    (∀ i, 0 < perturb p i) ∧
    (∀ i j, perturb p i ≤ perturb p j ↔ p i ≤ p j) ∧
    (∀ (σ : ListState n) (t : ℕ),
      expectedAfter (transpositionKernel p) σ t (excess p) ≤
        expectedAfter (transpositionKernel (perturb p)) σ t (excess (perturb p)) +
          ((t : ℝ) + 1) * (n : ℝ) ^ 2 * Real.exp (-(n : ℝ))) ∧
    entropyCeiling (stationaryLaw (perturb p)) ≤ (n : ℝ) ^ 3 / 2 := by sorry

end TranspositionIID.Main
